# A token for local development, so `npm run dev` can run the app's declared
# queries for real. Copy this file to `.env.local` (never commit it) and set
# VITE_BDA_TOKEN. `npm run dev` proxies /api to the service; which service
# decides which token you need.
#
# 1. Preview (the usual case: the app already exists in Bicycle Studio)
#
#    - Create the app first (MCP `dataapp_start`) and put its appId in
#      bda.manifest.json. Upload a version whose manifest declares the queries
#      you are working on: only declared queries run.
#    - Token: a Bicycle platform API token of your own (the one your MCP
#      connection uses; a person creates it in Bicycle). It runs queries as that
#      person, so treat it like a password: keep it in .env.local only.
#    - Start the dev server against preview:
#
#        BDA_API_ORIGIN=https://preview.bicycle.ai npm run dev
#
#    Functions, agents and workflows (`bda.fn`) do not run here: they need the
#    Studio host and answer `fn_unavailable`. Test them in the hosted app.
#
# 2. A local bicycle-studio service on localhost:8099 (the default target)
#
#    Mint a short-lived view token with the service's dev headers:
#
#      curl -s -X POST localhost:8099/api/data-apps/apps/<appId>/view-tokens \
#        -H 'X-Dev-User-Id: dev-user-0000-0000-0000-000000000000' \
#        -H 'X-Dev-Tenant-Id: dev-tenant' -H 'content-type: application/json' -d '{}'
#
#    View tokens are short-lived by design; re-mint when queries start failing
#    with token_expired.
VITE_BDA_TOKEN=
